      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at this NDA for a new fintech client and the \"residuals\" clause is a bit confusing. Can you help me figure out what this actually means for me? \n\n\"Recipient shall be free to use for any purpose the residuals resulting from access to or use of Confidential Information, provided that in all cases the Recipient shall maintain the confidentiality of the Confidential Information as provided herein. The term 'residuals' means information in non-tangible form, which may be retained in the unaided memory of persons who have had access to the Confidential Information.\"\n\nBasically, if i learn some specific ways to optimize their database queries or certain coding patterns while working there, am i allowed to use those same patterns for my other clients later? Or is that a violation?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
